MintCurveConvexPosition::repay(uint256)
├── given caller is not owner and not authorized spender
│   └── it should revert with MintCurveConvexPositionUnauthorized
└── given caller is owner or authorized spender
    ├── when repayShares is zero
    │   └── it should revert with MintCurveConvexPositionInvalidInput
    └── when repayShares is greater than zero
        ├── given repayShares exceeds the position's borrow shares
        │   └── it should revert
        ├── given the position balance plus owner funds cannot cover the required DUSD
        │   └── it should revert
        └── given enough DUSD is available
            ├── it should accrue interest before computing the required assets
            ├── given the position already holds enough DUSD
            │   └── it should repay without pulling from the owner
            ├── given the position holds insufficient DUSD
            │   ├── given caller is the owner
            │   │   └── it should pull the DUSD shortfall from the owner
            │   └── given caller is an authorized spender
            │       └── it should pull the DUSD shortfall from the caller
            ├── it should repay repayShares of debt on the mint market
            └── it should emit Repaid
